{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FHbbCTwHgMLpKs3wvhExQ5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor R&D Surface v11.1 â€” \"Handoff Always Primes\" â€” Execution Log\n2\t\n3\t> Foreman appends per-wave EXECUTE / ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW / FIX / JUDGE history here.\n4\t> Frozen design: `MASTER-PLAN.md`. Build plan: `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`.\n5\t> Branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v11.1` off master `b6719bd` (v11 merged, GREEN 1232).\n6\t> Baseline at branch cut: GREEN 1232, 1 skipped.\n7\t\n8\t<!-- Foreman writes below this line. -->\n9\t\n10\t## Wave 1 â€” Keystone: transcript snapshot + honest no-docs prompt (backend) â€” âœ… GREEN (3 iters)\n11\t\n12\t- **EXECUTE.** `prepare_stage_handoff` gains a synchronous transcript snapshot (D3/D4): when the initial persist produced no doc, read the source PTY buffer (`read_since(sid,0)`), clean it, write `<source_worktree>/<lane>/<sid[:12]>-transcript.md`, re-persist (session-tagged) â†’ the real doc-referencing prompt names it; best-effort never-raises; fires ONLY when no doc-classified file was produced. `handoff.build_next_stage_prompt` no-docs fallback rewritten HONEST + ACTIONABLE (\"create the materials\", no false \"report in worktree\"). New `tests/test_handoff_transcript_v11_1.py` + `tests/test_advance_research_to_plan_conversation_v11_1.py` (conversation-only: transcript seeded into the stub PTY buffer, NO file written; proven to FAIL pre-fix).\n13\t- **GATE 1.** GREEN 1239.\n14\t- **REVIEW (2 independent, refute) â€” SPLIT.** Reviewer A: GO (conversation-only test genuine + non-vacuous, best-effort, D4, scoped). Reviewer B: **the captured transcript is STUB-adequate but REAL-ConPTY-INADEQUATE** â€” the cleaner `\\r`-replace EXPANDS spinner redraws + only collapses blank lines â†’ on the live backend the transcript is dominated by redraw chrome, the Q&A buried (BLOCKER); the byte-exact seed-strip fails on rendered/wrapped output (leaves the load+greet boilerplate); the \"both\"/background-refine is DEAD in prod (gated on env `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY` which `main()` never exports â€” only the module flag); the 32KB tail-only cap drops the early research framing. **Judge: NO-GO** (green proves the plumbing, not the value â€” the exact stub-blind-spot v11 was meant to kill).\n15\t- **FIX iter 1.** Rewrote `_clean_transcript_text` into a 6-stage real-ConPTY pipeline (`\\r`-redraw frame-collapse â†’ broadened ANSI/CSI/OSC/DCS strip â†’ wrap-tolerant seed/greet strip â†’ box/spinner chrome drop â†’ dup-line collapse â†’ HEAD+TAIL cap). `anchor_gui.main()` now exports `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY=1` so the refine actually runs in prod (verified `main()` never runs in tests). New `tests/test_clean_transcript_v11_1.py` (raw-ConPTY-shaped input â€” FAILS pre-fix) + `tests/test_proactive_summary_gate_v11_1.py`.\n16\t- **FIX iter 2 (gate caught a regression the fix introduced).** GATE: `test_summary_on_finish_v7::test_kill_schedules_one_background_summary_non_blocking` failed under load â€” making the env gate LIVE exposed a real prod double-summary: killing a planning session fires the summary-on-finish hook AND (via auto-advance â†’ `prepare_stage_handoff`) the keystone background summary, both for the same session. Fix: `_trigger_background_source_summary` now SKIPS a TERMINAL source (DONE/FAILED â€” the finish hook owns it), still fires for a LIVE source (the transcript-refine case preserved). Deduped at the root; the v7 test passes even with env ON. New `tests/test_keystone_summary_dedup_v11_1.py`.\n17\t- **GATE 2 (orchestrator-run, of record).** `python -m pytest -q` (env unset) â†’ **GREEN 1254 passed, 1 skipped**.\n18\t- **VERDICT: GO.** Commit scoped (handoff.py, terminal_session.py, anchor_gui.py, tests/test_advance_artifacts_v10.py [honest-contract update], + 5 new v11.1 test files).\n19\t\n20\t## Wave 2 â€” Grass: always proceed + open the session (UI) â€” âœ… GREEN (2 iters, awaiting John's sign-off)\n21\t\n22\t- **EXECUTE.** Removed the `no-research-material` hard-refusal (effort_history.py ~817-822) so `advance_grass_research_to_plan` falls through to the v10 W5 contained-grass mint/focus/link machinery with the W1 transcript-backed prompt (or the honest-minimal \"create the materials\" for a truly-empty session); kept the `no-research-session` negative (nothing to advance FROM). anchor_gui `advanceGrassToPlan` drops the \"no materials\" toast. Updated 2 existing tests (test_grass_advance_v10, test_handoff_unified_v11) from asserting the refusal to the always-opens behavior (D1 change, not weakened). Mockup `_mockups/grass_advance_always.html`. New conversation-only backend + Playwright tests.\n23\t- **GATE 1.** GREEN 1259.\n24\t- **REVIEW (2 independent, refute).** Reviewer A: GO (guard removed, contained-grass wiring preserved verbatim, the empty-session-opens discriminator genuinely fails pre-W2). Reviewer B (probed the ORDERING): **BLOCKER** â€” develop-plan-FIRST + conversation-only: the transcript is committed to main HEAD and NAMED in the prompt, but the pre-existing plan worktree was cut BEFORE the commit â†’ the file is ABSENT from its checkout â†’ Crucible hits file-not-found. W2 turned a clean refusal into a silent broken handoff. Root: the grass advance wrote NO durable artifact into the plan worktree (unlike the non-grass path's HANDOFF.md/NEXT-PROMPT.md), and the tests asserted the path was NAMED, never on-disk.\n25\t- **FIX iter 1.** `effort_history._materialize_handoff_into_plan_worktree` â€” copies the persisted transcript/doc rels (from the main folder, guaranteed present via the W1 keystone) INTO the plan dev session's worktree + writes HANDOFF.md + NEXT-PROMPT.md there (matching the non-grass path); wired into BOTH the fresh-mint and focused-existing branches; best-effort never-raises; contained-grass wiring untouched. New `test_grass_advance_develop_plan_first_materializes_transcript` asserts `(plan_wt/rel).is_file()` for the develop-plan-first case â€” **proven to FAIL pre-fix** (file absent from the pre-existing worktree). Fresh-mint test extended with the on-disk + HANDOFF.md/NEXT-PROMPT.md asserts.\n26\t- **GATE 2 (orchestrator-run, of record).** `python -m pytest -q` â†’ **GREEN 1260 passed, 1 skipped**.\n27\t- **VERDICT: GO â€” committed to branch (9552049).** âœ… **John signed off 2026-06-20** (saw the grass research conversation advance to a plan session naming `research/<sid>-transcript.md` + \"read these first\"). Wave 2 done â€” John's reported grass failure is fixed.\n28\t\n29\t## Wave 3 â€” Healthcheck v11.1 + docs (PROJECT DONE) â€” âœ… GREEN\n30\t\n31\t- **EXECUTE.** `anchor_healthcheck.check_rnd_v11_1_surface` (registered in main()) walks the REAL conversation-only flow (fully stubbed; `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY` off+restored in the finally â€” load-bearing since the keystone now reads that env): (a) researchâ†’plan â€” seed the stub PTY buffer with transcript content (NO file/record_effort/kill), `prepare_stage_handoff`, assert the transcript is snapshotted+persisted+committed + the prompt names `research/<sid>-transcript.md` + idempotent; (b) grass â€” develop research dev session, seed the buffer, advance, assert it OPENS + the transcript is materialized ON DISK in the plan worktree + contained + linked. `tests/test_healthcheck_v11_1.py` (6, hermetic). CLAUDE.md v11.1 section.\n32\t- **GATE 1.** GREEN 1266.\n33\t- **REVIEW (1 closeout, additive wave).** **GO.** Verified: the healthcheck genuinely walks the real conversation-only flow (zero record_effort; asserts the transcript on-disk; a regression would fail it) â€” NOT a mask; hermeticity sound (the critical `ANCHOR_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY` save/restore present in the unconditional finally; no early-return skips it); docs map to shipped code with no overclaim (PROACTIVE_SUMMARY export correctly attributed to `anchor_gui.main()`); North Star delivered (both researchâ†’plan + grass snapshot the transcript, materialize it readable in the next worktree, never refuse); additive scope; distro clean.\n34\t- **GATE 2 (orchestrator-run, of record).** `python -m pytest -q` â†’ **GREEN 1266 passed, 1 skipped**.\n35\t- **VERDICT: GO â€” PROJECT DONE.** All 3 waves GREEN. The conversation-only handoff gap is fixed: advancing a research session that was a CONVERSATION (no written file) now snapshots the transcript, makes it readable in the next stage's worktree, opens the next session with an honest doc-referencing prompt, and never refuses â€” grass OR non-grass. Branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v11.1` ready for John's merge + deploy (no merge / no nssm restart until John signs off the whole branch).\n36\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"070dfe03-5de0-47a1-9dda-018bdf79b18f","uuid":"1430d851-2422-4049-9910-36b11674860e","timestamp":"2026-06-22T18:48:39.800Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\planning\\rnd-v11.1\\EXECUTION-LOG.md","content":"# Anchor R&D Surface v11.1 â€” \"Handoff Always Primes\" â€” Execution Log\n\n> Foreman appends per-wave EXECUTE / ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW / FIX / JUDGE history here.\n> Frozen design: `MASTER-PLAN.md`. Build plan: `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`.\n> Branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v11.1` off master `b6719bd` (v11 merged, GREEN 1232).\n> Baseline at branch cut: GREEN 1232, 1 skipped.\n\n<!-- Foreman writes below this line. -->\n\n## Wave 1 â€” Keystone: transcript snapshot + honest no-docs prompt (backend) â€” âœ… GREEN (3 iters)\n\n- **EXECUTE.** `prepare_stage_handoff` gains a synchronous transcript snapshot (D3/D4): when the initial persist produced no doc, read the source PTY buffer (`read_since(sid,0)`), clean it, write `<source_worktree>/<lane>/<sid[:12]>-transcript.md`, re-persist (session-tagged) â†’ the real doc-referencing prompt names it; best-effort never-raises; fires ONLY when no doc-classified file was produced. `handoff.build_next_stage_prompt` no-docs fallback rewritten HONEST + ACTIONABLE (\"create the materials\", no false \"report in worktree\"). New `tests/test_handoff_tr